Package: dstat
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), ${misc:Depends}
Description: versatile resource statistics tool
 Dstat is a versatile replacement for vmstat, iostat, mpstat, netstat and
 ifstat. It overcomes some of their limitations while adding extra features,
 more counters and flexibility. Dstat is handy for monitoring systems during
 performance tuning tests, benchmarks or troubleshooting.
 .
 This package is built from the maintained 0.8.x fork.  It includes the
 Python 3 fix for network counters that regress when virtual interfaces
 (veth/tap) disappear or are reset.
